    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a4198bb2-31d8-59be-937d-dcb7bb17c910",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2 t + 3,\\qquad y=t^{2} - 2,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-1)=2 \\left(-1\\right) + 3=1$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=\\left(2\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=2 t + 3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-2) &=2 \\left(-2\\right) + 3 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\left(0\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ |",
