      ":question/id": "7c2976c8-7e06-5251-922b-f103911b8f67",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2 - t^{2},\\qquad y=- 2 t,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=2 - \\left(-2\\right)^{2}=-2$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $4$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | $-4$ |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=- 2 t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=- 2 \\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $y=- 2 t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) &=- 2 \\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=2 - t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=2 - \\left(2\\right)^{2} \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $2$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-4$ |",
