      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t + 1}{t + 5},\\qquad y=t^{2} - t - 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} | $-1$ | $1$ |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=\\frac{t + 1}{t + 5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=\\frac{\\left(2\\right) + 1}{\\left(2\\right) + 5} \\\\ &=\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=\\frac{t + 1}{t + 5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-2) &=\\frac{\\left(-2\\right) + 1}{\\left(-2\\right) + 5} \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} - t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\left(0\\right)^{2} - \\left(0\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{1}{3}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $1$ |",
