      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t - 2}{t + 5},\\qquad y=t^{2} + t + 2,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{4}{3}$ | {{field-2}} | $- \\frac{2}{5}$ | $- \\frac{1}{6}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $2$ | $2$ | {{field-3}} | $8$ |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=\\frac{t - 2}{t + 5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=\\frac{\\left(2\\right) - 2}{\\left(2\\right) + 5} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=\\frac{t - 2}{t + 5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=\\frac{\\left(-1\\right) - 2}{\\left(-1\\right) + 5} \\\\ &=- \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} + t + 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) &=\\left(1\\right)^{2} + \\left(1\\right) + 2 \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{4}{3}$ | $- \\frac{3}{4}$ | $- \\frac{2}{5}$ | $- \\frac{1}{6}$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $2$ | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ |",
